{"description":"GitHub issue #35: Immutable plans have no usable retirement path in the CLI, while EKA guidance documents retirement as a sanctioned lifecycle step. Attempting transition to retired fails because planning-state table marks 'immutable' as terminal without outbound transitions, and `eka retire` command does not exist in the binary.","impact":"Superseded or stale immutable plans clutter active planning boards forever with no clean way to retire them without violating immutability invariants.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Expose sanctioned plan retirement path (e.g. `eka transition \u003cplan\u003e superseded` or add `eka retire` command per guidance).\n- Preserves history, relationships, and downstream traceability intact.\n- Clear error messages when attempting illegal transition on non-immutable or un-executed plans.\n- Conformance tests verify retired/superseded state can be queried via `eka get` / `eka view`.\n- Update CLI documentation to match."}